import{_ as n,o as i,c as a,a2 as t}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const v=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 829 | Transcended Ones and Civilization | Law Guarantees for Civilizational Innovation","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 829 | Transcended Ones and Civilization | Law Guarantees for Civilizational Innovation","no":829,"module":4,"tags":["Transcended One","Civilization","Civilizational Innovation","Law Guarantees","Trial-and-Error Room"],"related":["11-Deduction-Iteration System Detailed","10-Three-Hundred Origin Cultivation-Systems Overview","07-Self-Springing Self-Growing Evolution Laws"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0829_模块4-超脱者与文明-文明创新法则保障.md","filePath":"en/0829_模块4-超脱者与文明-文明创新法则保障.md"}'),o={name:"en/0829_模块4-超脱者与文明-文明创新法则保障.md"};function r(s,e,l,d,u,h){return i(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[t('<h1 id="entry-829-transcended-ones-and-civilization-law-guarantees-for-civilizational-innovation" tabindex="-1">Entry 829 | Transcended Ones and Civilization | Law Guarantees for Civilizational Innovation <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-829-transcended-ones-and-civilization-law-guarantees-for-civilizational-innovation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 829 | Transcended Ones and Civilization | Law Guarantees for Civilizational Innovation&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 4 · Transcendence Orthodox Definition Library | Benchmark base: Documents 11, 10, 07</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-civilization-does-not-die-from-making-mistakes-but-from-being-forbidden-to-make-them" tabindex="-1">Introduction: civilization does not die from making mistakes, but from being forbidden to make them <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-civilization-does-not-die-from-making-mistakes-but-from-being-forbidden-to-make-them" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: civilization does not die from making mistakes, but from being forbidden to make them&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The old system&#39;s handling of &quot;civilizational innovation&quot; is very contradictory: on one hand, the author needs the protagonist to &quot;innovate cultivation manuals&quot; and &quot;break through predecessors&quot; to drive the plot; on the other hand, the whole system&#39;s rules are fixed — innovation may only be the protagonist&#39;s patent; ordinary people are forbidden to touch it. The result of this contradiction: civilizational innovation completely depends on individual protagonists&#39; inspiration; the whole system&#39;s evolution is extremely slow. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s approach is entirely different: <strong>civilizational innovation is not the protagonist&#39;s patent, but Myriad Ranks&#39; right.</strong> The transcended one&#39;s work is not &quot;personally innovating then rewarding Myriad Ranks,&quot; but <strong>providing law guarantees for Myriad Ranks&#39; innovation — ensuring innovation has room, trial-and-error has protection, results have reward.</strong></p><p>Six top-level axioms in this entry centrally embody the republican axiom of Myriad Races: innovation right belongs to all Myriad Ranks, not monopolized in strong ones&#39; hands. The anti-predation axiom requires innovation results not be plagiarized by predators; the collective ascension axiom requires innovation&#39;s ultimate goal be pushing Myriad Ranks&#39; common evolution; the causal self-discipline axiom requires trial-and-error in the innovation process not disturb others; the law-first axiom requires innovation&#39;s law framework itself be self-consistent — innovation may trial-and-error, but may not violate fundamental laws.</p><p>The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><p>This article focuses: how the transcended one provides law guarantees for civilizational innovation.</p><h2 id="i-civilizational-innovation-s-four-directions" tabindex="-1">I. Civilizational Innovation&#39;s Four Directions <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-civilizational-innovation-s-four-directions" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Civilizational Innovation&#39;s Four Directions&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Per Three-Hundred Origin Cultivation-Systems Overview (Document 10) and Self-Springing Self-Growing Evolution Laws (Document 07), civilizational innovation unfolds in four directions:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Innovation Direction</th><th>Innovation Content</th><th>Guarantee Focus</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Cultivation-system innovation</td><td>New cultivation paths, new manual combinations, new realm understandings</td><td>Trial-and-error safety — innovators going into demonic obsession in trial-and-error have a safety net</td></tr><tr><td>Law-engineering innovation</td><td>New law application methods, new anchor technology, new energy-conversion paths</td><td>Patent protection — innovation results after publication are not plagiarized or monopolized</td></tr><tr><td>Social-organization innovation</td><td>New governance forms, new distribution methods, new education models</td><td>Institutional fault tolerance — social-organization-innovation failure does not hold the innovator accountable</td></tr><tr><td>Civilizational-experiment innovation</td><td>New plane-civilization experiments, new Myriad-Rank-symbiosis-model exploration</td><td>Isolation safety — experiments run in isolation spaces, not affecting the main civilization</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Four directions&#39; common point: <strong>innovation should have no &quot;ceiling&quot; — except that fundamental laws may not be violated, everything else may be explored.</strong></p><h2 id="ii-innovation-guarantees-three-laws" tabindex="-1">II. Innovation Guarantees&#39; Three Laws <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-innovation-guarantees-three-laws" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Innovation Guarantees&#39; Three Laws&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The transcended one provides three law guarantees for civilizational innovation:</p><ol><li><strong>Trial-and-error safety guarantee</strong>: cultivation-system innovation&#39;s demonic-obsession risk is real-time monitored by Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision — once an innovator during trial-and-error shows consciousness collapse or energy loss of control, the system automatically intervenes to protect. Trial-and-error may fail, but failure is not fatal.</li><li><strong>Result-reward guarantee</strong>: after innovation results are published, the innovator through the civilizational-weight mechanism receives continuous reward — his manual is used by Myriad Ranks; Myriad Ranks&#39; usage feedback and contribution values flow back to him through the household-contract responsibility mechanism. The innovator does not suffer.</li><li><strong>Intellectual-property guarantee</strong>: once innovation results are published, they enter the Selfless Dao public library — anyone may learn and use. But the innovator&#39;s authorship and contribution records are permanently retained. Publication does not mean being buried; contribution does not mean being swallowed.</li></ol><p>Three guarantees&#39; core logic: <strong>let innovators dare trial-and-error, have reward, not be buried.</strong> When these three conditions are met, Myriad Ranks&#39; innovation vitality will naturally be aroused.</p><h2 id="iii-why-innovation-needs-isolated-experimental-zones" tabindex="-1">III. Why Innovation Needs &quot;Isolated Experimental Zones&quot; <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-why-innovation-needs-isolated-experimental-zones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Why Innovation Needs &quot;Isolated Experimental Zones&quot;&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Among civilizational innovation there is a class of high-risk innovation — for example, a new cultivation system may cause large-scale demonic obsession; a new social-organization form may cause local social upheaval. Such innovation may not be directly trial-and-errored in the main civilization.</p><p>The solution is <strong>isolated experimental zones</strong>:</p><ul><li>Set up experimental zones in independent spaces or newly opened planes;</li><li>Innovators voluntarily enter experimental zones for innovative practice;</li><li>Between experimental zones and the main civilization there is a strict causal-isolation layer;</li><li>Experiments succeed, results are organized then promoted to the main civilization; experiments fail, losses are digested within the experimental zone, not affecting the main civilization.</li></ul><p>Isolated experimental zones&#39; design logic: <strong>innovation needs freedom, but freedom needs boundaries.</strong> Innovators may freely trial-and-error in experimental zones, but their trial-and-error may not drag the main civilization into the water. This is not limiting innovation, but protecting it — because if an innovator messes up in the main civilization, the whole civilization will blame innovation, and next time no one dares innovate. Isolated experimental zones let innovators trial-and-error boldly at ease, because they know the worst outcome also stays within the experimental zone.</p><h2 id="iv-the-transcended-one-s-role-in-innovation-guarantees" tabindex="-1">IV. The Transcended One&#39;s Role in Innovation Guarantees <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-the-transcended-one-s-role-in-innovation-guarantees" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. The Transcended One&#39;s Role in Innovation Guarantees&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The transcended one&#39;s role in civilizational-innovation guarantees is <strong>guarantor, not innovator</strong>:</p><ul><li>He does not stipulate &quot;what should be innovated&quot; — innovation directions naturally arise from Myriad Ranks&#39; needs and inspiration;</li><li>He does not evaluate &quot;whether innovation is good&quot; — innovation&#39;s value is naturally tested by Myriad Ranks in use;</li><li>He provides &quot;innovation&#39;s safe environment&quot; — trial-and-error safety, result reward, intellectual property three law guarantees;</li><li>He maintains &quot;innovation&#39;s infrastructure&quot; — isolated experimental zones&#39; construction, public knowledge library maintenance, Alaya Network&#39;s monitoring of trial-and-error.</li></ul><p>What the transcended one does is &quot;build roads&quot; work — he builds, guards, and direction-marks innovation&#39;s roads, but which road to take and how fast is the innovator&#39;s own matter.</p><h2 id="v-five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">V. Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><p><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: isolated experimental zones ensure innovation trial-and-error losses are controlled locally, not causing large-scale waste in the main civilization</p></li><li><p><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: intellectual-property guarantees institutionally seal the predatory channel of &quot;strong ones plagiarizing innovators&#39; results&quot;</p></li><li><p><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang-Luo innovation is the protagonist&#39;s patent, ordinary people are forbidden to touch; Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s innovation is Myriad Ranks&#39; right; the transcended one only provides guarantees</p></li><li><p><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: three law guarantees open to all Myriad-Rank innovators; no matter what race, what background, whoever has innovation may enjoy guarantees</p></li><li><p><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: four innovation directions, three law guarantees, and isolated-experimental-zone mechanism are all publicly queryable; Myriad Ranks may supervise whether the guarantee system is fair</p></li><li><p>Terminology alignment: the Balanced Anchor Hyper-Multiverse Realm is this batch&#39;s standard realm appellation; the Myriad-Origin two-way cycle ensures energy and knowledge circulate perpetually among Myriad Ranks; exercise of law-anchor authority is strictly constrained by four-dimensional assessment and democratic procedure.</p></li><li><p><strong>Axiom 6 · Universal Equal Infinite Law</strong>: all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will not be eliminated by the times; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity — infinite origin inherent in all; predation naturally loses its meaning</p></li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Law guarantees for civilizational innovation is the republican axiom of Myriad Races&#39; institutional fulfillment at the civilizational-development dimension. The transcended one does not innovate for Myriad Ranks; he builds roads for Myriad Ranks&#39; innovation. Trial-and-error has a safety net, results have reward, intellectual property has guarantee, high-risk has isolation zone — when these four guarantees are in place, Myriad Ranks&#39; innovation vitality will well up like a spring. The transcended one knows: civilization evolves not by some protagonist&#39;s inspiration, but by millions of Myriad Ranks&#39; continuous innovation. What he must do is let every one of these millions&#39; innovations be safe, worthwhile, and not buried.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/11-推演迭代体系详解.html">Entry 11 · Deduction-Iteration System Detailed</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/10-三百套本源修炼体系总览.html">Entry 10 · Three-Hundred Origin Cultivation-Systems Overview</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/07-自生自长进化法则.html">Entry 07 · Self-Springing Self-Growing Evolution Laws</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/826_模块4-超脱者与文明-总论.html">Entry 826 · Transcended Ones and Civilization Overview</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',30)])])}const m=n(o,[["render",r]]);export{v as __pageData,m as default};
